NO GAME ASSETS OR EXTRACTED GAME DATA ARE REDISTRIBUTED
-------------------------------------------------------

This repository contains and redistributes NO game assets and NO extracted game
data of any kind. That includes, without limitation: textures, models, audio,
animations, UI art, fonts, localization tables, datatables, blueprints, and any
content unpacked from the game's shipped archives.

This is trivially true rather than merely a policy statement: the game's Unreal
Engine 5 .pak archives are AES-encrypted, so nothing is extractable to begin
with. There is no asset pipeline in this project because there can be none.

Any numeric values that appear in this project - stat coefficients, scaling
curves, breakpoints, and similar - are independently derived from observed
in-game behavior and from publicly published community documentation. Observed
behavior and protocol facts are not themselves copyrightable; shipped content
is, and none of it is here.


WHAT THIS PROJECT READS
-----------------------

Lanternlight reads only files that the game itself writes into user-writable
locations on the operator's own machine - for example the log and save tree the
game creates under the local application data directory. It does not decrypt,
unpack, patch, inject into, or otherwise modify the game or its installed files,
and it does not read from the game's installation directory.

Those game-written files can contain personally identifying information such as
account identifiers, persona names, session tokens, and geolocation inferred
from an IP address. None of that is committed to this repository, and the
repository's ignore rules and pre-commit hook are configured to keep it out. If
you fork or run this project, treat anything copied out of the game's save tree
as sensitive and keep it local.
